+## Act 21 / Act 28 and suite-compliance classification
+- **Act 21 (Change Quality Gate, enacted):** `§1` a green, exact commit+tree suite run is required before `git push` for `government/**` or `tests/**`; `§2` forbids GitHub-hosted CI as the authoritative agent-execution environment (not at issue); `§3` requires machine-readable `records/suite-status.json` recording `base_commit`, `head_commit`, `tree`, `passed`, etc.; `§5` “satisfies the green-test requirement before push for that exact candidate change”, `landed_commit` and `verification_basis` recorded; `§6` Judiciary measures `green_suite_compliance_rate` over main commit+tree from suite-status records. (source: `government/LAWS.md` Act 21, inspected in immutable `/tmp/opencode/viche-origin-main-7727`.)
+- **Act 28 (Verified-Change Landing, enacted):** `§1` “verified candidate” satisfies Act 21 for the exact candidate commit/tree before any push/fast-forward; `§2` records verification basis and later landed identity; `§3` preserves exact commit/tree when the landed branch fast-forwards to the verified candidate (or documents squashed reconstruction); `§4` post-landing `records/suite-status.json` recorded by Clerk after landing.
